## Conclusion

The only value is $\boxed{c = 4}$.

- **Necessity:** $\mu(X) = c < \infty$ forces the range to be symmetric about $c/2$. The symmetry conditions $c - 1 \in [3,c]$ (from $1 \in R$) and $[0, c-3] \subseteq [0,1] \cup [3,c]$ (from $[3,c] \subseteq R$) together force $c = 4$.
- **Sufficiency:** The measure space $([0,1] \sqcup \{p\},\, \mu)$ with Lebesgue measure on $[0,1]$ and an atom of mass $3$ at $p$ achieves range $[0,1] \cup [3,4]$.

